{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1493537-source-material-for-alternate-settings","id":1493537,"title":"Source material for alternate settings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-22T15:57:02-07:00","id":1493537,"title":"Source material for alternate settings?","content":"I've been listening to the audiobooks of S. M. Stirling's alt-history <i>The Black Chamber</i>, <i>Theater of Spies</i>, <i>Shadows of Annihilation</i>, and <i>Treasures of Tatary</i> (not yet released in audiobook). The conceit is that Taft dies in 1912 and Theodore Roosevelt wins the presidency, dramatically remaking America in a way that seems quite good in many ways, but is showing some disturbing signs towards tyranny. Then Germany essentially wins the Great War in 1916 using nerve gas attacks. This seems like a really good alt setting for a Continuum type setting. It's got protagonists and some antagonists that really feel like they're Talents. There's some super-science, too; nothing really extreme but classic &quot;borrowing from the future&quot; such as radar appearing in 1916 rather than 1939. Restricting to talents would pretty well nail the level of protagonist ability. Another S. M. Stirling is his one-off <i>The Peshawar Lancers</i>, which has some psi in it along with protagonists that feel, again, quite Talent-like. The psi is very Flux-like. Even if one doesn't want to use the settings wholesale there might be some good examples. Any others that look really worthwhile?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2173-jvv","name":"JVV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T09:10:07-07:00","id":1493580,"title":"","content":"As far as alternate histories go, <a href=\"http://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/AltEarths/\" target=\"_blank\">GURPS Alternate Earths</a> (volumes 1 and 2) has several interesting possibilities. From a Trinity Continuum perspective, especially that of Adventure!, the best one is the world of <i>Gernsback</i>. It's point of divergence is built around Nikola Tesla marrying JP Morgan's daughter, Anna (the two were platonic friends in the real world), and her stabilizing influence and financial support helped make a number of his ideas - including wirelessly broadcast electrical power - a reality. The result is an alternate 1965 with advanced retro-futuristic technology (flying cars, for example, are common, but no one has invented the transistor yet), a fairly powerful League of Nations, and a lot of social aspects still in their pre-WW2 forms.<br /> <br /> If you want something weirder, with a sort of surreal semi-Cyberpunk flavor, there's the world of <i>Shikaku-Mon</i>. It's 2015 and the world is divided between four great powers: A Westernized and Christianized Japanese Empire; a totalitarian &quot;synarchist&quot; Swedish Empire; a fairly progressive Empire of Brazil; and very technologically advanced Kingdom of France.<br /> <br /> Alternately, if you want some good enemies to fight, volume 1 also includes <i>Reich-5</i> (the Axis win WW2 after FDR is assassinated in 1933) and <i>Dixie</i> (a victorious Confederacy in 1985). Also included are <i>Roma \u00c6terna</i> (a somewhat industrialized global Roman Empire in what would be our 1878) and <i>Ezcalli</i> (an Aztec dominated world).<br /> <br /> Volume 2 includes the worlds of <i>Centrum</i> (the main villain of the GURPS Infinite Worlds/Time Travel settings; what was a world dominated by a unified Anglo-French empire turned into a post-nuclear war world now dominated by a totalitarian military-industrial cabal based out of Australia), <i>Midgard</i> (Vikings successfully colonized the New World), <i>Caliph</i> (an ultra-tech Islamic dominated world), <i>Cornwallis</i> (Britain defeated the American revolution), <i>Ming-3</i> (an Imperial Chinese dominated world), and <i>\u00c6olus</i> (kind of hard to sum up, with a Catholic resurgence in England, and a bunch of republican revolutions in Europe, resulting in a world with a lot of modern tech - except airplanes, for some reason - but fairly antiquated political thought).<br /> <br /> If you want to get even odder, there's GURPS Technomancer, in which the first atomic tests brought back magical energy into the world, resulting in a sort of open urban fantasy setting. It's probably pretty easy to swap out a lot of the magic and fantasy tropes with Flux and various Psi and/or flux-tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T11:47:15-07:00","id":1493590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JVV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1493537-source-material-for-alternate-settings#post1493537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been listening to the audiobooks of S. M. Stirling's alt-history <i>The Black Chamber</i>, <i>Theater of Spies</i>, <i>Shadows of Annihilation</i>, and <i>Treasures of Tatary</i> (not yet released in audiobook). The conceit is that Taft dies in 1912 and Theodore Roosevelt wins the presidency, dramatically remaking America in a way that seems quite good in many ways, but is showing some disturbing signs towards tyranny. Then Germany essentially wins the Great War in 1916 using nerve gas attacks. This seems like a really good alt setting for a Continuum type setting. It's got protagonists and some antagonists that really feel like they're Talents. There's some super-science, too; nothing really extreme but classic &quot;borrowing from the future&quot; such as radar appearing in 1916 rather than 1939. Restricting to talents would pretty well nail the level of protagonist ability. Another S. M. Stirling is his one-off <i>The Peshawar Lancers</i>, which has some psi in it along with protagonists that feel, again, quite Talent-like. The psi is very Flux-like. Even if one doesn't want to use the settings wholesale there might be some good examples. Any others that look really worthwhile?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want more alternative settings that start at the beginning of the 20th century, I suggest these for inspiration: <a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kaiserreich_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Kaiserreich</a>, <a href=\"https://kingart-games.com/games/7-iron-harvest/game\" target=\"_blank\">Iron Harves</a>t, and <a href=\"https://imagecomics.com/comics/series/carbon-grey\" target=\"_blank\">Carbon Grey</a>. If you want something a bit more magic oriented, there's also <a href=\"https://imagecomics.com/comics/series/arrowsmith\" target=\"_blank\">arrowsmith</a>. For more ideas, I suggest this <a href=\"https://gizmodo.com/11-intriguing-ways-world-war-i-could-have-turned-out-di-1652195903\" target=\"_blank\">article</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T15:32:47-07:00","id":1493602,"title":"","content":"Arrowsmith is an awesome war story. It\u2019s magical, sure, but it shows how horrible war is and how you can be the bad guy in the others stories\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}